# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Firebase Authentication — SMS OTP (real SMS for EVERY country)
# 1) Create a project at https://console.firebase.google.com
# 2) Project settings → General → "Your apps" → Web app (</>) → copy the config
# 3) Authentication → Sign-in method → enable "Phone"
# 4) Authentication → Settings → Authorized domains → add localhost (default) and your production domain
# 5) Paste the values below (remove the leading "# " from each line you fill):
# VITE_FIREBASE_API_KEY=AIza...
# VITE_FIREBASE_AUTH_DOMAIN=your-project.firebaseapp.com
# VITE_FIREBASE_PROJECT_ID=your-project-id
# VITE_FIREBASE_STORAGE_BUCKET=your-project.appspot.com
# VITE_FIREBASE_MESSAGING_SENDER_ID=1234567890
# VITE_FIREBASE_APP_ID=1:1234567890:web:abcdef123456
# Active local development configuration for Firebase project e6-dac9d.
VITE_FIREBASE_API_KEY=AIzaSyB-kcD96YymqD0MkLxLUXEv8ztOekqqxYQ
VITE_FIREBASE_AUTH_DOMAIN=e6-dac9d.firebaseapp.com
VITE_FIREBASE_PROJECT_ID=e6-dac9d
VITE_FIREBASE_STORAGE_BUCKET=e6-dac9d.firebasestorage.app
VITE_FIREBASE_MESSAGING_SENDER_ID=947369057236
VITE_FIREBASE_APP_ID=1:947369057236:web:35cc9d10deee10bf131441
#
# With these set, the mobile-number login + onboarding recovery phone send the
# code via Firebase SMS (all countries). If they are empty, the app falls back
# to the existing WhatsApp OTP flow automatically.
# Restart `npm run dev` after changing this file.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------